# Xcode
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

# Model weights. These are gigabytes and are downloaded into the app sandbox,
# not into the repository — the patterns are here as a backstop for anyone who
# drops one in by hand. Deliberately not `Models/`, which would also swallow
# Sources/PocketdKit/Models.
*.gguf
*.safetensors

# Editor and OS cruft
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Upstream and competitor checkouts read while building this: other people's
# repositories under their own licenses, never vendored. The script that
# fetches them is committed; what it fetches is not.
reference/*
!reference/sync.sh
!reference/README.md

# Agent worktrees
.claude/

# Competitor screenshots kept for reference, like reference/. Thirty megabytes
# of someone else's app UI does not belong in a public repository — the notes
# taken from them are in docs and the plan, which is the part with any value.
NewUI&FeatureMocks/

# App Store and marketing work — listing copy, competitor analysis, store
# screenshots, the compositor that builds them, and anything staged to shoot
# them with. None of it is the product, and this is a public MIT repository
# whose README already carries the screenshots a reader needs.
#
# It lives outside the checkout entirely (../pocketd-store) rather than being
# ignored in place, so that it cannot be added by a wildcard or a `git add -A`.
# These patterns are a backstop for the case where someone drops one back in.
docs/store/
docs/app-store-listing.md
scripts/store-shots.py
store-assets/
*-store-shots/
